# Dev scratch scripts
#
# R132: this rule silently voided the evidence rule. Every number in this
# project must name a producer path (Law 2) — and `_*.py` made every producer
# named with a leading underscore UNCOMMITTABLE. I0's commit landed its ten
# .json outputs and dropped ALL NINE of its .py producers without a word, so
# its report cited scripts a fresh clone would never receive.
#
# Nobody wrote that contradiction deliberately. It assembled itself from two
# reasonable decisions: "ignore scratch scripts" and "cite your producer".
#
# harness/notes/** is the producer directory and is now exempt. Producers are
# named <leg>_<name>.py going forward — I1 renamed its own from _i1_*.py to
# i1b_*.py on discovering this, unprompted, which was the right instinct.
_*.py
!__init__.py
!python/synapse/mcp/_tool_registry.py
!harness/notes/**/_*.py
!harness/verify/**/_*.py
!**/__init__.py
_*.ps1
_*.txt
houdini_exec.py
nul

# Logs
*.log

# Manual tests
tests/manual_*

# MkDocs build output
site/

# Houdini temp files
*.hip/
*.hiplc/
*.hipnc/
backup/

# Secrets and media
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.jpg
*.png
# ...except design EVIDENCE. A before/after screenshot set is the product of a
# design leg, not incidental media, and a blanket *.png silently swallows it —
# the reviewer sees a receipt claiming shots that are not in the tree. Narrow
# exemption: this one directory, produced by harness/notes/panel_shot.py.
!design/repair_h4/**/*.png

# Claude Code local settings (permissions, session-specific)
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Synapse runtime memory (auto-generated by Living Memory in Houdini)
claude/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendored dependencies (Sprint 3 Spike 2.2)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# python/synapse/_vendor/ holds pip-installed anthropic + transitive deps
# (pydantic-core with its .pyd, httpx, httpcore, etc.). The outer rules
# above ignore *.pyd, *.py[cod], *.so, and _*.py â€” all of which would
# catch vendor contents. Whitelist the whole vendor tree explicitly and
# then re-ignore only the build artefacts we never want committed.
!python/synapse/_vendor/
!python/synapse/_vendor/**
python/synapse/_vendor/**/__pycache__/
python/synapse/_vendor/**/*.pyc

# SCOUT reconnaissance artifacts (read-only investigation output)
.scout/

# FORGE build-orchestration artifacts (run logs, specs)
.forge/

# close-the-loop harness run artifacts
.close-the-loop/

# H22 prep harness â€” bundle archives + transient check-debug dumps (never tracked)
/H22_prep_harness.zip
/houdini22prepareHarness_v2.zip
.claude/checks_debug_*.txt
harness/notes/_prov_live.json
# API-delta probe run artifacts (regenerated per run; drop-day outputs)
.claude/probe_delta.json
.claude/probe_delta.md
.claude/mcp_surface_delta.json
harness/state/wheel_cache/

# harness/state local runtime â€” the *.example templates ARE tracked; these real
# files are per-machine, not shared project truth. drop = local H22 capture
# (harness/CLAUDE.md designs for its absence -> live fallback); posture = local
# deployment posture; *_readiness_verdict = generated check output.
harness/state/drop.json
harness/state/posture.json
harness/state/release_readiness_verdict.json
harness/state/studio_readiness_verdict.json
harness/state/recovery/
# transient per-run stderr logs (torch/pynvml warnings, harness probe output)
harness/state/*.err

# docs/ research + debug scratch â€” scraped page dumps and node-diagnostic debris,
# never shared project truth
docs/*.txt
docs/nca_*
# (was an enumeration losing a race: nca_*, debug.txt, cop_diag.txt, and 15 more.
#  Zero docs/*.txt
docs/nca_* are tracked, so a blanket rule is safe. L0.F12.)

# Release-week demo captures (Leg 1) â€” raw screen recordings, never tracked
demo/captures/

# R47 measurement instrument - supplies the shipping interpreter's missing deps.
# Regenerate with harness/supply_shipping_deps.ps1; never a substitute for vendoring.
.hython_deps/
.pytest_bt_*/

# C1 token benchmark raw payload dumps (multi-MB; the counted summary is
# committed under harness/notes/c1/ instead)
.c1out/
.c1smoke/
